Z||000000||Uaana||06-18-2001||09:16 PM||||Left my GT with the GF to get rear calipers thrown on today. (Simply because no one has a caliper rebuild kit around here) So<BR>A. They charge 106 US per caliper +50 core.<BR>B. Total bill 580US.. hmmm 380 labor to put calipers on? The rears were already removed<BR>all the stick had to do is drop the new ones on and connect the hose and parking brake cable... Shouldn't take more than an hour.. So how in the hell could it come up to more thatn 300 labor????||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||06-18-2001||09:31 PM||||Thats outrageous!  Did they put new rotors on too?  I had a quote of $800 for the rear brakes on my Formula.  They included over $100 for each rotor on top of the $100+ per caliper!!  Labor was about half the quote too.  Needless to say I ended up doing the work myself.  Saved the rotors and rebuilt the calipers myself.  Saved a ton, and I know it wasn't done poorly.||||reg||1
